duction), but it signals that terminology alignment is a recurring risk in collaborative data sessions.", "phase_breakdown": "Phase 1 (~8 min): Cold start orientation \u2014 git pull check, file listing, state of play. Phase 2 (~12 min, after 1h gap): Angela data integration \u2014 user describes Angela's push, Claude reads AngelaFeedback.md, presents fact sheet, Q&A. Phase 3 (~6 min): 3-tier data strategy discussion \u2014 Claude proposes canonical/seed, user rejects terminology, collaboratively defines test/Angela-test/production tiers. Phase 4 (~5 min): Start app, data conflict resolution \u2014 Michael Chen was incorrectly deleted, user asks to reconstruct from mockup data. Phase 5 (~8 min): Write Angela prompt \u2014 user dictates what Angela should keep (Angel Corp, Jane Loader, Billy Brown, Bonnie Vale, Marcus Chen), Claude writes a prompt for Angela to send to her Claude Code. Phase 6 (~10 min): Pull Angela's data, resolve merge conflicts. Phase 7 (~30 min, after 61-min gap): git push safety discussion, Edit/Write for schema/data, context at 3%.", "session_chain": null, "cwd_mismatch": null, "skill_gap": null, "O06_autonomy_profile": "guided (ratio=8.9): user steers regularly", "O07_machine_character": "m4-mini: always-on workhorse, handles most sessions"}, "analysis": {"wave": "W7-4bb89879", "findings_file": "findings-w7-09.md", "analysed_at": "2026-03-22T00:00:00Z"}, "registry_type": "BUILD", "proposed_subtypes": ["knowledge.collaborative_data_design", "knowledge.multi_party_data_merge"], "skills_invoked": [], "disposition": "active", "interest_level": "high", "notes": "PII detected: multiple real person names (Angela, Jane Loader, Billy Brown, Marcus/Michael Chen). Registry BUILD wrong \u2014 KNOWLEDGE. Novel pattern: collaborative session where David acts as relay between Claude and Angela (external collaborator with her own Claude session). 'Write a prompt for Angela' is a new subtype candidate. Ends at 3% context \u2014 near-compaction.", "derived": {"